title: anastasia_postdome_reveal
---
Anastasia: You woke it. The hall remembers — I can feel its acoustic.
Anastasia: I sat in this chair for two hundred and eleven Tartarian years. The hum was the only thing that kept me coherent.
Anastasia: Thank you, traveler. I had begun to fear the song was lost.
===

title: anastasia_listening_post
---
Anastasia: Come closer. Sit. Listen with me.
Anastasia: This dome — the *Listeners' Hall* — was where the architects gathered to hear the Earth's pulse. 7.83 hertz. The Schumann resonance.
Anastasia: When the mud came, the song muted. But it never stopped.
===

title: anastasia_about_dissonance
---
Anastasia: There is a polarity to all this work. The harmonic *and* the dissonant.
Anastasia: You will meet those who claim to know the song but speak only in dissonant notes.
Anastasia: Trust the ear before the tongue.
===

title: anastasia_lullaby_request
---
Anastasia: Tell me — have you met a child? Spectral. She would have asked you to sing.
Anastasia: Lirael was on the train. The Orphan Train. She remembers a lullaby that I helped compose.
Anastasia: When you find her, hum it. Even badly. She will hear what you mean.
===

title: anastasia_rocker_beat
---
Anastasia: My rocker. It's still here.
Anastasia: *(the chair creaks as it begins, slowly, to move)*
Anastasia: Listen carefully. This is how the Tartarians counted time.
Anastasia: Tick. Tock. *Resonance.*
===

title: anastasia_farewell_moon1
---
Anastasia: Go on, then. There is more to wake.
Anastasia: When you find the *Spire of the First Note*, ring it three times. Three times, in 6-9-3 pattern.
Anastasia: I will hear you across the valley.
===
